course: dictionary
lesson: 1232
title: Bullock and the farm words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to a special group. A bullock is one of the words about farm animals. When a word is about one special thing, the words near it often tell you what it is. «Only female cattle give milk, from the udder, the bag under the tummy: «cow» means a female, males are bulls or bullocks, the young are calves and a group is a herd.» Here the sentence sorts the cattle into groups, so a bullock must be one kind of male cattle.
explain: Look at the clues in the sentence. A cow is a female. A bull is a male. A bullock is also a male, but it is not a bull. It is a young male cow that has had its parts removed, so it cannot father calves. That is why farmers raise bullocks for beef.
explain: Stories use words like bullock to show a place. A bullock cart creaking down a dusty road tells the reader that we are on a farm, or in a village far from the city. The word gives you a picture before the author describes anything else. Use the clues around the word to build that picture.
fact: A bullock is a young male cow that has been castrated, which means it cannot father calves.
fact: Bullocks are usually raised for beef, which is meat.
fact: In the United States, bullock can also mean a young bull.
fact: In some countries, such as India, bullocks pull carts and ploughs.
fact: Cattle words: a cow is a female, a bull is a male, a calf is a young one, and a herd is a group.
exercise: «The farmer led the bullocks across the field.» What is a bullock? | *A young male cow that cannot father calves | A baby horse | A female cow that gives milk | A wooden cart
exercise: In a story, «the old bullock cart creaked along the dusty road.» What does this tell the reader? | We are in a busy city full of cars | We are out at sea | *We are on a farm or in a rural place | We are in space
exercise: «Males are bulls or bullocks, and the young are calves.» Which word means the young of a cow? | bull | udder | herd | *calf
test: Which word means a group of cattle? | Calf | *Herd | Bullock | Udder
test: In the United States, what does bullock mean? | A young cow that gives milk | A farm gate | A bullock cart | *A young bull
exam: Farmers often raise bullocks. Why? | *For beef, which is meat | For eggs | To make milk | For wool
